{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/189564-utterance-dice-pools","id":189564,"title":"Utterance Dice Pools","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-06T13:09:29-07:00","id":189564,"title":"Utterance Dice Pools","content":"In going over the utterance mechanics, I noticed that the dice pools tend to be somewhat haphazard. Some use a Pillar + Sekhem format for the activation roll, while other use a the Attribute + Skill + Pillar format. In other cases, they use a simple Attribute + Skill pool. This seems to be all over the place, and in the case of the Sekhem-based pools and non-Pillar-based pools, the Arisen seem to be left at a distinct disadvantage compared to other supernaturals. Was there a particular rationale for what utterances used a specific format, or was this an oversight in terms of mechanics standardization?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T15:32:41-07:00","id":190805,"title":"","content":"Id assume that the ones with Sekhem are meant to fluctuate between very powerful when the mummy rises to very weak before it passes into slumber, while the others are meant to be more reliable until the descent renders them unusable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title"